1. Component Breakdown
   What it is: @omid2007hope/autotheme (v1.7.0) — a zero-dependency JavaScript/TypeScript + React theming engine (src/index.js, src/react/useAutoTheme.js).
   What it does: Evaluates time, day-of-week, date-range, and exact-date rules to return or apply CSS classes, inline style objects, or CSS custom properties.
   How it works: compile() buckets rules by priority; resolveRule() resolves the highest-priority match against a Date; observe(), autoVars(), and useAutoTheme() sync on minute boundaries and visibilitychange.
   Why it exists: Eliminates manual Date / timer / SSR hydration boilerplate for time- and season-aware UI styling.
2. Findings (Bugs, Problems, Missing Items & Enhancements for v1.8)
   🔴 Bugs & Logic Flaws

autoVars() 3rd parameter mismatch causes an infinite ~1ms timer loop

Exact Lines: src/adapters/css-vars.js:45 & src/adapters/css-vars.js:72-76 vs. README.md:156 & src/types/index.d.ts:66-68, src/types/index.d.ts:172-176.
Problem: README.md and index.d.ts pass { interval: 60000 } (an object) as the 3rd argument, but autoVars(cssEntryArray, target, interval = 60000) treats interval as a raw number. Passing { interval: 60000 } makes Date.now() % interval evaluate to NaN, causing setTimeout and setInterval to fire continuously every ~1ms.

Broken import { compile } in src/types/index.d.ts

Exact Lines: src/types/index.d.ts:1 and src/types/index.d.ts:148-150.
Problem: Line 1 has import { compile } from "../core/engine"; while line 148 redeclares export declare function compile. When copied into dist/index.d.ts and dist/react/useAutoTheme.d.ts (package.json:28), ../core/engine does not exist (TS2307) and collides with the local compile declaration (TS2440).

TypeScript declarations reject CompiledRules<T> from compile()

Exact Lines: src/types/index.d.ts:103, src/types/index.d.ts:148-150, src/types/index.d.ts:160-163, src/types/index.d.ts:172-176, src/types/index.d.ts:198-202.
Problem: auto(), useAutoTheme(), observe(), autoVars(), and compile() are typed to only accept AutoRule<T>[] (or AutoVarRule[]), not CompiledRules<T>. Following the pre-compilation pattern in README.md:253-262 produces a TypeScript type error.

Incomplete since/until rules with time or day hijack daily rules instead of warning

Exact Lines: src/core/engine.js:176-200.
Problem: else if (eachRule.time != null) (line 176) and else if (eachRule.day != null) (line 191) come before else if (eachRule.since != null || eachRule.until != null) (line 195). A rule missing until like { since: '12-01', time: 18, style: 'winter' } never reaches line 195; it is silently pushed into timeRules and activates every day of the year at 18:00.

day constraint is silently ignored on date and since/until rules

Exact Lines: src/core/engine.js:103-163, src/core/engine.js:187-189, and src/core/utils.js:235-253.
Problem: A composite rule like { since: '06-01', until: '08-31', day: [0, 6], style: 'summer-weekend' } is placed in dateRanges, where resolveRule() only checks isInDateRange(r, now) and never checks isDayMatch(r, now).

isEqual() in useAutoTheme.js has two false-positive bugs

Exact Lines: src/react/useAutoTheme.js:42-56.
Problem:
Line 42 checks if (Array.isArray(a)) but does not reject if (Array.isArray(b)) return false; when a is a non-array object and b is an array.
Lines 53–55 iterate for (const key of keysA) and call isEqual(a[key], b[key]) without checking Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(b, key). If a is { time: undefined } and b is { date: undefined }, a['time'] and b['time'] are both undefined, returning true.

autoVars() leaves stale CSS variables on the DOM when rules stop matching

Exact Lines: src/adapters/css-vars.js:52-59.
Problem: if (!matched || !matched.vars) return; (line 54) exits before the cleanup loop (lines 57–59). When a date-specific or day-specific rule expires and resolveRule() returns null, its previously injected CSS variables are never removed from the target element.

observe() crashes on null/missing config and fails to clean up when switching between class strings and style objects

Exact Lines: src/core/observer.js:37-45 and src/core/observer.js:66-90.
Problem:
Line 40 destructures config without a default config = {}, throwing a TypeError if observe() is called without arguments.
Lines 67–88 only clean up previousStyle if its type (string vs object) matches nextStyle. Transitioning from an inline style object rule to a class string rule leaves the inline styles on the element (and vice-versa).

observe() / applyClasses() strips pre-existing classes from the target element

Exact Lines: src/adapters/dom.js:19-24 and src/core/observer.js:123-124.
Problem: If the target element originally had a class (e.g., flex or text-black) before observe() was called, and a rule also includes that class, el.classList.remove(...toRemove) removes the host's original class when transitioning to another rule or calling controller.stop(), contradicting README.md:294.

Loose date, time, and day validation in compile(), parseDate(), and parseTime()

Exact Lines:
src/core/engine.js:104-113 & src/core/engine.js:131-140: isValidDate only checks dateStr.length >= 4 && dateStr.length <= 10. Non-hyphenated strings/numbers like { date: 20271031 } (length 8) pass validation without warning and get pushed to exactRecurring.
src/core/utils.js:23-44: parseDate() does not check !isNaN(...) or valid calendar bounds (month 1–12, day 1–31), so "foo-bar" or "99-99" returns { month: NaN, day: NaN } or { month: 99, day: 99 }.
src/core/engine.js:150-193: since, until, and day are never validated in compile(), so invalid ranges or invalid day names ({ day: 'funday' }) never emit console.warn.
src/core/utils.js:158-179: parseTime() uses parseInt without checking full numeric format or parts.length === 2, so "10:20pm" silently parses as 10:20, "12px" as 12:00, "-0:30" as 00:30, and floats like time: 6.3 parse as 6.3 \* 60 = 378 (06:18).

Mixed-format since/until date range (YYYY-MM-DD with MM-DD) silently ignores the year

Exact Lines: src/core/utils.js:131-142.
Problem: if (since.year != null && until.year != null) requires both endpoints to have a year; if only one has a year, it silently degrades to an annual recurring MMDD check.

useAutoTheme() crashes if options is null

Exact Lines: src/react/useAutoTheme.js:59-64.
Problem: const { interval = 60000 } = options; throws a TypeError if a caller passes null as the 3rd argument (options = {} only defaults undefined).
🟠 Build, Packaging & Type Declaration Problems

Root and ./react entry points copy the exact same .d.ts file, exposing wrong exports on each

Exact Lines: package.json:28 and src/types/index.d.ts:148-202.
Problem: Copying src/types/index.d.ts to both dist/index.d.ts and dist/react/useAutoTheme.d.ts tells TypeScript that useAutoTheme is exported from @omid2007hope/autotheme (it is not in src/index.js:8-10) and that auto, compile, autoVars, observe are exported from @omid2007hope/autotheme/react (they are not in src/react/useAutoTheme.js:59).

Build script prepends a duplicate 'use client'; directive

Exact Lines: src/react/useAutoTheme.js:1 and package.json:28.
Problem: src/react/useAutoTheme.js already has "use client"; on line 1, and the build script prepends 'use client';\n again to dist/react/useAutoTheme.js and dist/react/useAutoTheme.cjs.

auto() 3rd parameter (now?: Date) is missing from TypeScript declarations

Exact Lines: src/types/index.d.ts:160-163 vs. src/core/engine.js:223 and README.md:302.
Problem: README.md:302 documents passing an explicit now Date to auto(), which engine.js:223 supports, but index.d.ts:160-163 omits now?: Date.
🟡 Missing Pieces, Dead Code & Documentation Mismatches

Missing test coverage for useAutoTheme, applyClasses, observe, and autoVars

Exact Lines: src/react/useAutoTheme.js:1-140, src/adapters/dom.js:1-33, src/core/observer.js:69-135, src/adapters/css-vars.js:50-101.
Problem: README.md:6 displays a 100% TEST COVERAGE badge, but useAutoTheme.js has zero tests, and observer.js (inline style objects, CSS vars in inline styles, selector lookup, stop() teardown, visibilitychange) and css-vars.js have only a single basic smoke test in tests/ssr-rendering.test.js:24-63.

day rule feature is completely undocumented in README.md and missing from warning text

Exact Lines: README.md:79-95 and src/core/engine.js:204.
Problem: Day-of-week rules (day: 'friday' | [0, 6]) are implemented in engine.js and utils.js, but missing from the Rule Object Shape table (README.md:79-88), the Priority Resolution diagram (README.md:89-95), and the invalid-rule warning in src/core/engine.js:204.

Unused imports and dead isSsr() function

Exact Lines:
src/core/engine.js:9-16: isExactDateMatch, isInDateRange, getMatchingTimeRule, and isDayMatch are unused imports.
src/adapters/css-vars.js:9-14: isExactDateMatch and getMatchingTimeRule are unused imports.
src/core/utils.js:12-14: isSsr() is unused across src/, and its test in tests/utils.test.js:146-149 says it('returns false...') while asserting true.

Stale documentation & badges in README.md and corrupted characters in tests/bugfix.test.js

Exact Lines:
README.md:1: Hard-codes version 1.6.4 in the Socket badge URL.
README.md:244-246: Claims useAutoTheme uses JSON.stringify under the hood, whereas src/react/useAutoTheme.js:38-57 uses recursive isEqual.
README.md:358: States "Contribution guidelines will be published with the v1.0 stable release".
tests/bugfix.test.js:262 & tests/bugfix.test.js:288: Contains corrupted UTF-8 replacement characters (``).

Leftover scratch and temporary files in the repository

Exact Lines: test.ts:1, scratch/fix_test.cjs:1-26, .todo:1-195, and .npmignore:1-9 (redundant with "files": ["dist"] in package.json:24-26 and has a typo ReadME on line 9).
🟢 Enhancements for v1.8

Avoid redundant DOM mutations on every tick in autoVars()

Exact Lines: src/adapters/css-vars.js:50-65.
Enhancement: Track previousVars (similar to previousStyle in src/core/observer.js:57-66) so tick() skips removing and re-setting all CSS custom properties every 60 seconds when the active rule has not changed.

Pre-parse date, since, until, and day in compile()

Exact Lines: src/core/engine.js:95-100 and src/core/utils.js:70-151.
Enhancement: compile() currently pre-computes \_minutes, but parseDate() (split('-') + parseInt) and DAY_MAP string lowercasing still run on every auto() call. Pre-computing \_date, \_since, \_until, and \_days inside compile() makes runtime evaluation zero-allocation and validates all fields once up front.

Support CSS selector strings for target in autoVars()

Exact Lines: src/adapters/css-vars.js:46 vs. src/core/observer.js:47-49.
Enhancement: Allow target in autoVars(rules, '#app') to accept a CSS selector string just like observe() does.

Add TypeScript type-checking to CI

Exact Lines: .github/workflows/ci.yml:27-31 and package.json:27-31.
Enhancement: Add tsc --noEmit to npm test / ci.yml so broken .d.ts declarations cannot slip into a release
